{"id": "85841", "name": "ספליין קובי – פולינום מחבר שגזיר ברציפות (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Consider the real function</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(x) :=\\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} {{CT:0}} &amp; \\mbox{for } x\\leq {{CT:1}}, \\\\ p(x) &amp; \\mbox{for } {{CT:1}} &lt; x &lt; {{CT:2}}, \\\\ {{CT:3}} &amp; \\mbox{for } {{CT:2}}\\leq x.\\end{array} \\right. \\]</p><p style=\"text-align:center\">{{CT:4}}</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find the cubic polynomial \\(p(x)\\) which makes \\(f(x)\\) continuously differentiable.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(p(x)=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> For \\(f\\) to be continuously differentiable, \\(p\\) must match the values and the derivatives of the outer pieces at both junction points; these four conditions determine the four coefficients of the cubic.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The conditions on \\(p\\)</b><br><p>First we need to find the information which \\(p(x)\\) needs to satisfy. This is</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p({{CT:1}})={{CT:5}}. \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p({{CT:2}})={{CT:6}}. \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p'({{CT:1}})={{CT:7}}. \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p'({{CT:2}})={{CT:8}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The linear system for the coefficients</b><br><p>If we define \\(p(x)\\) to be the cubic</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p(x) = a_3 x^3 + a_2 x^2 + a_1 x + a_0, \\]</p><p>We then set up the matrix equation</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:9}} {{CT:10}} = {{CT:11}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The polynomial</b><br><p>Solving this gives the coefficients, from which we get the polynomial.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ p(x)={{CT:12}} \\]</p><p>We can view this as</p><p style=\"text-align:center\">{{CT:13}}</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 30, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "anspt : if (x>x0 and x<x1) then ans1 else 1000;", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "subst(x=x0,ans1)", "tans": "subst(x=x0,f0)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0.25, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer does not satisfy \\({{CT:14}}\\).</div>"}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "subst(x=x1,ans1)", "tans": "subst(x=x1,f1)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0.25, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "prt1-2-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "prt1-2-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer does not satisfy \\({{CT:15}}\\).</div>"}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "subst(x=x0,diff(ans1,x))", "tans": "subst(x=x0,diff(f0,x))", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0.25, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "prt1-3-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "prt1-3-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer does not satisfy \\(p'({{CT:1}})={{CT:7}}\\).</div>"}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "subst(x=x1,diff(ans1,x))", "tans": "subst(x=x1,diff(f1,x))", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0.25, "nextnode": 4, "answernote": "prt1-4-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": 4, "answernote": "prt1-4-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer does not satisfy \\(p'({{CT:2}})={{CT:8}}\\).</div>"}}, {"name": 4, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "degree(ans1,x)", "tans": "3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": 5, "answernote": "prt1-5-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": 5, "answernote": "prt1-5-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is not a cubic!</div>"}}, {"name": 5, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-6-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is plotted below. {@plot([pg,anspt],[x,(x0-3),(x1+3)],[y,-3,3])@}</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-6-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is plotted below, although part of your graph might appear out of range of the plot! {@plot([pg,anspt],[x,(x0-2),(x1+5)],[y,-3,3])@}</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["CS", "CS2", "CT", "CV", "f0", "f1", "pg", "ta", "tapt", "x0", "x1"], "nvariants": 1}